(I) Find the functional relationship between $y$ and $x$;
(II) Please budget: What is the maximum total cost for the company's training this time?

response:
(I) When $0 \leq x \leq 30, x \in \mathbb{N}$, $y = 400x + 1000x = 1400x$;
When $30 < x \leq 60, x \in \mathbb{N}$, $y = 400x + [1000 - 20(x - 30)]x = -20x^2 + 2000x$.

Thus, the function relationship between $y$ and $x$ is defined as:
$$
y =
\begin{cases}
1400x, & \text{when } 0 \leq x \leq 30, x \in \mathbb{N} \\
-20x^2 + 2000x, & \text{when } 30 < x \leq 60, x \in \mathbb{N}
\end{cases}
$$

(II) When $0 \leq x \leq 30, x \in \mathbb{N}$, $y \leq 1400 \times 30 = 42,000$ yuan, where $x = 30$;
When $30 < x \leq 60, x \in \mathbb{N}$, $y \leq -20 \times 50^2 + 2000 \times 50 = 50,000$ yuan, where $x = 50$.

In conclusion, the company's maximum total cost for the training this time is $\boxed{50,000 \text{ yuan}}$.

